# ALTN 2 FAIL: alternator 2 gives no current while alternator 1 carries both buses (format 1). The checklist (heading, message, rows and comment rows) is reproduced as printed in the DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist, Edition 4.1 of 2022-10-05 (owner decision 2026-10-23); all other text is own wording. The weights and the forbidden items are instructor-review values.
format: 1
id: elec-altn2-fail
title: ALTN 2 FAIL
source:
  document: "DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist"
  issue: "Edition 4.1, 2022-10-05"
  section: AFM 03A-02 ALTN 2 FAIL
  verified: "2026-10-23"
disclaimer: training-aid
scene: cruise
briefing:
  situation: "You are in cruise flight when the yellow ALTN 2 FAIL message appears on the primary flight display. The second Amps pointer has dropped to zero. The engine runs normally and the bus voltage is normal."
initial:
  quantities:
    alt2_amps: 0
    alt2_fault: 1
parameters:
  alt2_output: 0
annunciations[1]: altn_2_fail
checklist:
  form: table
  heading: ALTN 2 FAIL
  message: ALTERNATOR 2 HAS FAILED
procedure[5]:
  - kind: group
    id: breaker_check
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: alt2_breaker_in
        severity: critical
        number: 1
        text: Circuit breaker
        action: check IN
        done:
          check: state
          control: cb.alt2
          is: in
  - kind: group
    id: immediate
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: alt2_off
        severity: critical
        number: 2
        text: Alternator 2
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.alternator_2
          is: off
  - kind: line
    number: 3
    text: Bus voltage
    action: MONITOR
  - kind: comment
    text: Terminate NVFR/IFR-flight and land at nearest suitable airfield.
  - kind: comment
    text: Leave icing conditions.
# Each of these removes the remaining supply of the buses; both are instructor-review items. Essential bus ON is not graded: it is harmless here.
forbidden[2]:
  - id: alt1_off
    text: Switch off alternator 1
    fails_run: true
    trigger:
      check: state
      control: sw.alternator_1
      is: off
  - id: elect_master_off
    text: Switch off the electrical master
    fails_run: true
    trigger:
      check: state
      control: sw.elect_master
      is: off
# No outcome: an ignored ALTN 2 FAIL only costs the additional loads, alternator 1 carries both buses through the closed tie relay, so nothing escalates and the run fails by its missed critical steps alone.
# The four causes behind the one message, as for ALTN 1 FAIL: the alternator is dead and the breaker in; the breaker has popped and the alternator is fine; the alternator has a short and its breaker pops again when it is pushed in; the breaker has popped and the alternator is dead too, so pushing it in does not help. The checklist above is the printed one; which of its rows are graded depends on the cause drawn at the start of a run. The weights and the cause texts are instructor-review values.
variants[4]:
  - id: alternator_dead
    weight: 40
    applies[1]: alt2_off
    debrief: The breaker was in and alternator 2 had failed.
  - id: breaker_popped
    weight: 30
    controls:
      cb.alt2: out
    parameters:
      alt2_output: 1
    applies[1]: alt2_breaker_in
    debrief: The alternator 2 circuit breaker had popped. Pushing it in cleared the message.
  - id: alternator_shorted
    weight: 15
    controls:
      cb.alt2: out
    parameters:
      alt2_short: 1
    applies[1]: alt2_off
    debrief: Alternator 2 had a short and its circuit breaker had popped. Pushing the breaker in only popped it again, so the alternator had to be switched off.
  - id: breaker_popped_dead
    weight: 15
    controls:
      cb.alt2: out
    applies[1]: alt2_off
    debrief: The alternator 2 circuit breaker had popped and the alternator was dead as well. Pushing the breaker in did not help.
# The failure of the level Realistic begins at a random second inside this short window; the window is an instructor-review value.
onset:
  window_s[2]: 2,6
